From ed0c536dde2bab4de8414fee74f7c45f94adfc87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:05:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] custody v2: extract the daemon's sealed-state writer (no
 behavior change)

The serialized host writes (saveNow), the chain checkpoint store, the member store and the platform host-policy store
move verbatim into custody/v2/sealed-state.mjs so the exact persist path can be tested. Same semantics: the member and
host-policy saves are still fire-and-forget; the next commit adds the durability barrier.
---
 custody/v2/daemon.mjs       | 11 ++++++-----
 custody/v2/sealed-state.mjs | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 custody/v2/sealed-state.mjs

diff --git a/custody/v2/daemon.mjs b/custody/v2/daemon.mjs
index 3ae7d7bf1bad072a8e9b02d0dac8c1279edaf330..a2c2dbc00b63e86246fae2a1f31ea0393ed5ccea 100644
--- a/custody/v2/daemon.mjs
+++ b/custody/v2/daemon.mjs
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
